<div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(56px,10vh,120px) clamp(20px,5vw,56px) 0;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(83% 0.05 80);margin:0 0 24px;">Brand & positioning · Insights</p><h1 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,5.4vw,72px);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin:0 0 32px;max-width:18ch;">Have you outgrown your brand?</h1><p style="font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(88% 0.015 60);margin:0;">DsignPoint · November 2026 · 4 min read</p></div>
</section>
<section style="background:oklch(97% 0.012 70);padding:clamp(32px,5vh,64px) 0 0;"><div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;aspect-ratio:16/8;"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="../../uploads/ins_outgrown.webp" alt="Old printed brand materials beside fresh burgundy and champagne colour swatches on a sunlit table" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 62%;"></div></div></section>
<section style="background:oklch(97% 0.012 70);padding:clamp(48px,8vh,88px) 0 clamp(64px,10vh,120px);"><div class="art" style="width:100%;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);"><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,30px);line-height:1.4;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 44px;">Your brand probably wasn’t wrong when you built it. It fit the business you were then: the services you offered, the clients you served, the ambition you had. The real question is whether it still fits the business you are now.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Growth changes what a business is</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Businesses rarely stand still. The offer becomes more focused, or more ambitious. Prices rise. The ideal client changes. A founder who started by doing everything starts leading a team. Meanwhile the logo, the website and the way you describe yourself were fixed on day one, and quietly stayed there.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">La Casita Bilingual School is a good example. A well-established school with a full waitlist and a strong local reputation, its website simply didn’t reflect that quality. Nothing about the school had got worse. Its online presence had just stopped keeping up, so we restructured the site around the visitor and gave it a clear path to enrolment. <a href="../../case-studies/la-casita/" style="color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);border-bottom:1px solid oklch(33% 0.14 17);white-space:nowrap;">See the La Casita case study →</a></p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">That gap is what we mean by outgrowing a brand. It doesn’t mean the brand is bad. It means it is describing a business that no longer exists.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Six signs the gap is real</h2><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">01</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">You explain yourself more than you should</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">If your sales conversations start with correcting what people assumed from your website, the site is selling a smaller or different business than the one you actually run.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">02</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">You attract the wrong clients</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">Enquiries come from people who want the cheapest option, or who expect something you stopped offering. Your positioning is speaking to the wrong audience.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">03</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">Your website describes who you were</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">It lists services you have outgrown and says very little about the work you actually want more of.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">04</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">You look smaller than you are</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">Competitors with less experience come across as more established. Your results are real, but your presentation isn’t carrying them.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">05</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">Your offer is hard to summarise</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">Services accumulated over the years, and you can’t say in one sentence what you do or who it is for. If you can’t, your customers can’t either.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 38px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 8px;">06</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,2.5vw,30px);line-height:1.15;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:0 0 10px;">You hesitate to send the link</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0;">A high-value prospect asks where they can learn more, and you feel a small wince before sharing your website. That feeling is worth listening to.</p></div><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">If you recognised three or more of these, it is worth looking closer. If you only recognised one, you may have a messaging issue rather than a brand issue.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">The quiet cost of waiting</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">An outdated brand rarely fails loudly. It costs you quietly: the prospects who never get in touch, the proposals that get negotiated down because you didn’t look the part, the referrals that need extra explaining. Because none of it appears as a line item, it is easy to keep postponing.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Not every sign means a rebrand</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">This is where many businesses go wrong. They recognise a few of these signs and jump straight to a new logo. But the cause is often one layer deeper. It might be positioning that was never updated, an offer that grew without structure, or a website that simply needs restructuring. Sometimes it is a genuine brand evolution. Sometimes the brand is fine and the message isn’t. Occasionally the right call is to change nothing.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">In practice we usually see one of four outcomes: the message needs sharpening, the offer needs simplifying, the website needs restructuring, or the brand itself needs to evolve. Often it is a mix, and the order matters. Evolving a brand is also not the same as starting over. The best evolutions keep what is still true, like recognition and trust, and update what no longer reflects the business.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">A new visual identity on top of unclear positioning is just a more attractive version of the same confusion.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">Three questions to answer first</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Before you commission anything, try answering these honestly:</p><div style="background:oklch(93% 0.015 60);padding:clamp(28px,4vw,52px);margin:32px 0 40px;"><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,29px);line-height:1.25;color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);margin:0 0 22px;">Who is the business for now, specifically? Not who it was for when you started.</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,29px);line-height:1.25;color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);margin:0 0 22px;">What do you do today that you didn’t do before, and what have you stopped doing?</p><p style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,29px);line-height:1.25;color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);margin:0 0 0px;">What do you want to be known for in three years?</p></div><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Take your time with these. The first answer is usually the broadest, and the useful one comes after you have pushed on it. “Small businesses” is not an audience. “Founder-led service businesses ready to charge for their expertise” starts to be one.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Then read your website with those answers beside it. The distance between what you just wrote and what the site says is your brief.</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.01em;color:oklch(17% 0.014 30);margin:60px 0 22px;">What to do with the gap</h2><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">Once you can see the gap, the next step is deciding how much of it matters right now. Some gaps are cosmetic. Others are costing you clients every week. The work is to prioritise: what should change first, what can wait, and what should stay exactly as it is.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">A simple place to start: write one sentence describing your business as it is today, and put it next to your homepage headline. If they don’t match, you have found your first priority.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 24px;">You don’t necessarily need more. You may need different. And finding out which one is true is where it starts.</p><p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:44px 0 0;">Not sure where your business stands? <a href="../../book-a-call/" style="color:oklch(33% 0.14 17);border-bottom:1px solid oklch(33% 0.14 17);">Tell us where you are today</a> and we’ll help you see it clearly.</p></div></section>
<section style="background:oklch(93% 0.015 60);padding:clamp(56px,9vh,100px) 0;"><div style="width:100%;max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5vw,56px);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:clamp(24px,4vw,64px);align-items:center;"><a class="img-z" href="../start-with-your-business/" style="flex:1 1 360px;aspect-ratio:4/3;"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="../../uploads/ins_start.webp" alt="A notebook with hand-drawn sketches, coffee and glasses on a sunlit terrace table by the sea" style="object-position:center 70%;"></a><div style="flex:1 1 360px;"><p style="font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:oklch(52% 0.09 70);margin:0 0 24px;">Keep reading</p><h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader Variable','Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,46px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin:0 0 18px;"><a class="ttl" href="../start-with-your-business/">We don’t start with your brand. We start with your business.</a></h2><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:oklch(28% 0.02 30);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:44ch;">Most agencies begin with a service request. We begin with a question about your business. Here’s why, and what it changes about the way we work.</p><a class="rd" href="../start-with-your-business/">Read the article <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
